        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$(x^{3})^{4} = x^{7}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Added instead of multiplied. Correct: $x^{12}$",
          "worked": "Multiply the indices instead of adding them: $(x^3)^4=x^{3\\times4}=x^{12}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "index-t3-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(a^{5})^{2} = a^{25}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Squared instead of multiplied by 2. Correct: $a^{10}$",
          "worked": "Multiply 5 by 2 instead of squaring it: $(a^5)^2=a^{5\\times2}=a^{10}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "index-t3-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$(b^{2})^{6} = 2b^{12}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "There is no 2 in front. Correct: $b^{12}$",
          "worked": "The 2 is an index, so it does not become a coefficient: $(b^2)^6=b^{2\\times6}=b^{12}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
